  "query": "I finally have about 120 dollars saved for my first mechanical keyboard after years on a mushy laptop-style board. I split my time between office writing all day and playing shooters at night, and I'm stuck between a cheaper hot-swappable board that leaves money for nicer switches later, or blowing the whole budget on a well-known prebuilt. I honestly don't even know whether linear or tactile switches suit someone like me, or what people who bought each option ended up regretting. What actually matters at this price, and what would you put in the cart if you were me?",
